Patch summary:
RenderEngine no longer ends SurfaceFlinger when a buffer cannot be imported
as a texture. GaneshBackendTexture aborted ("Failed to create a valid
texture") whenever the driver could not wrap an AHardwareBuffer, so one bad
buffer from one app restarted SurfaceFlinger and every app with it; Ika has
hit this on virtual GPUs twice (H.264 frames under Venus on Intel, and a
Vulkan RenderEngine missing import extensions). Now:
- such a texture is logged and stays invalid; makeImage() and makeSurface()
  return nothing for it instead of asking Skia (a buffer with no size is
  still fatal, as that is a programming error);
- AutoBackendTexture takes a reference only for an image or surface that
  was made, since Skia calls no release proc for one that was not;
- drawLayersInternal leaves a layer without a texture out of the frame and
  fails the composition (BAD_VALUE) when the output buffer has none, and the
  gainmap path fails the same way.
DSA (desktop-subsystem-for-android) makes the same change in its
frameworks/native patch 0005.

diff --git a/libs/renderengine/skia/AutoBackendTexture.cpp b/libs/renderengine/skia/AutoBackendTexture.cpp
index 84357f1..ffefaa2 100644
--- a/libs/renderengine/skia/AutoBackendTexture.cpp
+++ b/libs/renderengine/skia/AutoBackendTexture.cpp
@@ -64,8 +64,11 @@ sk_sp<SkImage> AutoBackendTexture::makeImage(ui::Dataspace dataspace, SkAlphaTyp
     SFTRACE_CALL();
 
     sk_sp<SkImage> image = mBackendTexture->makeImage(alphaType, dataspace, releaseImageProc, this);
-    // The following ref will be counteracted by releaseProc, when SkImage is discarded.
-    ref();
+    // The following ref will be counteracted by releaseProc, when SkImage is discarded. A
+    // texture the driver could not import makes no image, and so no releaseProc call.
+    if (image) {
+        ref();
+    }
 
     mImage = image;
     mDataspace = dataspace;
@@ -80,7 +83,10 @@ sk_sp<SkSurface> AutoBackendTexture::getOrCreateSurface(ui::Dataspace dataspace)
         sk_sp<SkSurface> surface =
                 mBackendTexture->makeSurface(dataspace, releaseSurfaceProc, this);
         // The following ref will be counteracted by releaseProc, when SkSurface is discarded.
-        ref();
+        // A texture the driver could not import makes no surface, and so no releaseProc call.
+        if (surface) {
+            ref();
+        }
 
         mSurface = surface;
     }
